; The side a double does not protect. Winning 42 p. 11 (S-0024-b), p. 101
; (S-0133-h) and p. 94 (S-0125-d); the bidding hands of Ch. 2
; (Hands 10 and 11).
; Claim, in our words: the bidder's double of a suit protects his off on that
; side only; led in its other suit the off is exposed. In Hand 29 the 3-3
; covers the 3-2's trey side and the setters take it on the deuce side; with
; both sides covered (Hand 10's 4-3 under the 4-4 and the 3-3) an off risks
; nothing; in Hand 11 the 3-3 does not cover the 2-0 when deuces are led. In
; Hand 27 the 6-2 off risks one trick (its ten is trump, the 2-2 covers the
; deuces) and the 3-1 is open on its ace side but risks no count there (the
; 4-1 is trump).
; Reading: (out o c) as off-risk.silas, kept to the suits o follows in which
; the bidder holds no double: a double follows only its own suit, and under
; doubles trump none.

(include book)

(query (out o c)
  (pattern
    (viewer b)
    (bidder b)
    (mine o)
    (not (trump-tile o))
    (not (double o))
    (count-tile o)
    (same o c)
    (some (roles q) (in o q) (none (roles d) (mine d) (double d) (in d q))))
  (pattern
    (viewer b)
    (bidder b)
    (mine o)
    (not (trump-tile o))
    (not (double o))
    (live c)
    (not (mine c))
    (count-tile c)
    (some (roles q) (in o q) (in c q) (none (roles d) (mine d) (double d) (in d q)))))
